07d1daa54ad58cf04feee07adedad66d4c806b5f88d.svg) as ![](images/f9/f9b318487299434d45096742eaad8ea148abb88c27b718c1bc0983f927dc9911.svg)\n\n5\\. The domain is ![](images/04/043681a7084203dcb8609f78989cadb8f0bcd701978361940d93ef850da95a14.svg), and the range is ![](images/95/95d0bc38cd8737723521d2a1846cb71a0dba33d3df26bd73c18acbb650fc8b95.svg)\n\nThese key points apply to *any* exponential curve ![](images/90/90517bb7bc12cfec9d00d88592bbda7572f4a0c5cbcf4f66049311d42f20f6ca.svg) with ![](images/e2/e276af13a21df7f4755de7b18da1a10ca590bbdf3387515efa0896f6cddb79cf.svg) These graphs always have the same general shape:\n\n![](images/0f/0f8e7cc0db94f5f51bc83404351a7708171fdce50e2946b51263885e4230ecef.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111827 #edb/ref 1065 1544 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111827 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "6e919c9a-e896-5b0b-8570-5a7a377146d3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111827 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111828 #edb/ref 1064 "Multiplying an exponential decay function by a positive number **scales** the graph in the vertical direction.\n\nFor example, the curve ![](images/d5/d59881254ee1a66445dcf2697e8af4426cbe9d219443d5f40ef2aefc426d598b.svg) represents a vertical scaling of ![](images/fb/fb1255ff2ad78ef15b03968cb806543d4f29f1029680068f76c913bb4cab96ad.svg) by a factor of ![](images/27/270d33581e0657a10d567c6cfaa529521b34e20a39c9a29550698cbf252fabfa.svg)\nIt takes all of the ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg)-coordinates on ![](images/fb/fb1255ff2ad78ef15b03968cb806543d4f29f1029680068f76c913bb4cab96ad.svg) and multiplies them by ![](images/27/270d33581e0657a10d567c6cfaa529521b34e20a39c9a29550698cbf252fabfa.svg) This has the effect of **stretching** the curve upwards.\n\n![](images/d5/d5cf96822f65e51d618b651174f1c516eb97be3bf61f5b1380d1c245d29a5a72.png)\n\nNotice that the horizontal asymptote at ![](images/b3/b3259a74b1b63f2b49841acd0eea4f599e9dacf9c4f1b17bda0a3cb115a9d90e.svg) remained the same, and the ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg)-intercept moved from ![](images/42/42f562f132f08838fe095cdeb883c38dd65e0d77828f65f73d783980c52f34ec.svg) to ![](images/43/437619dfcf8db5be350de504dc9d98eab13c2ac21c62998d3c268a1f475a30d9.svg)\n\nOn the other hand, the curve\n![](images/99/99f750a011acdbe86e9c9397d5e5901c686a2c10b625fa9dc98a0b90a516c592.svg)\nrepresents a vertical scaling of\n![](images/c8/c8c077b168d3c60c74b354ee942893abefb51b5e08b7483044ea5ea2edf50795.svg)\nby a factor of ![](images/31/31659384627c9aa2540de6fca01634acdcdd4c77dd705fbf922c813cc23e822f.svg) It takes all of the ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg)-coordinates on ![](images/c8/c8c077b168d3c60c74b354ee942893abefb51b5e08b7483044ea5ea2edf50795.svg) and multiplies them by ![](images/31/31659384627c9aa2540de6fca01634acdcdd4c77dd705fbf922c813cc23e822f.svg) This has the effect of **compressing** the curve downwards.\n\nIn general, for *any* vertically stretched or compressed exponential curve ![](images/8c/8ccfcf186ac190ccb8f91676958e6030b4224bfd46b3598261736fbfcb7c351f.svg)\n\n- the horizontal asymptote at ![](images/b3/b3259a74b1b63f2b49841acd0eea4f599e9dacf9c4f1b17bda0a3cb115a9d90e.svg) remains the same, and\n\n- the ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg)-intercept moves from ![](images/42/42f562f132f08838fe095cdeb883c38dd65e0d77828f65f73d783980c52f34ec.svg) to ![](images/e8/e8c4c8598a8228afb25cbf13c034e2fe234393f9b9c0dfde8be1726b4fc79a8e.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111828 #edb/ref 1065 1545 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111828 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "4ea28190-d93f-521e-964b-cdd4aad84f69" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111828 #edb/ref 1067 "Vertical Stretching and Compression" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390340 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186390341 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390340 #edb/ref 1069 "q-18